# Shell scripts must keep LF endings — they are COPY'd into Linux Docker
# images and exec'd. On Windows, core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite
# them to CRLF, making the `#!/bin/sh` shebang unresolvable (exec: no such
# file or directory). Force LF regardless of platform / git config.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Other Linux-container assets that are line-ending sensitive.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
